  "seminaryName": "St. Vincent de Paul Regional Seminary",
  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "There is no winter, only a week in January when the Cubans wear coats and the Canadians swim.",
      "Summer is a thunderstorm every afternoon at four, and the pastor learns to schedule the funerals for the morning.",
      "Hurricane season is a cone on the television and a run on plywood, and the parish hall becomes a shelter before the chancery asks.",
      "The mornings in March are the reason people came, and the traffic on US-1 is the reason they complain."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "The Spanish Mass at noon is the biggest thing in the parish and it starts at twelve-fifteen, by long custom, whatever the bulletin says.",
      "The Creole Mass in Little Haiti runs two hours and the choir would run three; the collection is small bills and a great deal of joy.",
      "In Coral Gables the ushers wear guayaberas and the collection is discreet, in envelopes, and large."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The priests of Miami speak Spanish at dinner and English at the chancery, and the ones who cannot do the first are quietly pitied.",
      "Half of them were ordained for another diocese on another continent and are still explaining how they came to be here.",
      "They know the traffic better than the breviary and can name the three overpasses that will make a man late to a funeral."
    ]
  },
